-# The order in which a source-backed PRIM evaluates its actuals: the written
-# order of the source body they borrow from, not the order of the input slots.
-# The slots are the primitive's ABI (a send's Ref stands last among its
-# inputs although it is written first); the source body is the one physical
-# record of the written order, and lmx_walk_source_find already numbers its
-# nodes in that order. `firsts` and `order` are the caller's n cells each:
-# firsts[i] receives slot i's first ordinal, order the n slot indices, each
-# once, sorted by that ordinal; an absent slot has ordinal 0 and evaluates
-# nothing wherever it stands. lmx_walk_prim_source_check has proved every
-# present actual to be one owned node of this source.
